<title>USA: ResMed gets FDA okay on apnea device.</title>
<headline>ResMed gets FDA okay on apnea device.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>ResMed Inc saidFriday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has given 510(k) clearance to its AutoSet Home device for the treatment of obstructive sleep apnea.</p>
<p>According to the company, AutoSet Home is intended for the long-term treatment of obstructive sleep apnea in the home, and uses ResMed's patented technology for detection of inspiratory flow limitation and snoring.</p>
</text>
